#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:3
msgid "JSON output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:5
msgid ""
"Most pipx commands accept ``--output json`` to print a single machine-"
"readable result envelope on stdout instead of human-readable text. Selecting "
"JSON suppresses the normal progress messages, so the envelope is the only "
"thing on stdout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:11
msgid "Envelope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:13
msgid ""
"The envelope is a JSON object with these keys (serialized with sorted keys):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:19
msgid "Key"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:20
msgid "Value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:21
msgid "``pipx_result_version``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:22
msgid "Envelope schema version, currently ``\"1\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:23
msgid "``command``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:24
msgid ""
"The command tokens as a list, for example ``[\"install\"]`` or ``[\"cache\", "
"\"dir\"]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:25
msgid "``status``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:26
msgid ""
"``\"success\"`` when there are no errors, ``\"partial\"`` when the run both "
"succeeded somewhere and recorded errors, ``\"error\"`` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:28
msgid "``exit_code``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:29
msgid "The integer process exit code (see :doc:`exit-codes`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:30
msgid "``data``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:31
msgid "Command-specific payload object. Its fields depend on the command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:32
msgid "``errors``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:33
msgid ""
"List of error objects. Each has ``code``, ``message``, and the optional "
"identity fields ``environment`` and ``package``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:36
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"pipx_result_version\": \"1\",\n"
"  \"command\": [\"install\"],\n"
"  \"status\": \"success\",\n"
"  \"exit_code\": 0,\n"
"  \"data\": {},\n"
"  \"errors\": []\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:47
msgid ""
"A dispatch failure on a JSON-enabled command still speaks the envelope: it "
"prints a ``status`` of ``\"error\"`` with a single error whose ``code`` is "
"``pipx_error``, and exits ``1``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:52
msgid "Supported commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:54
msgid ""
"``--output json`` is available on: ``install``, ``inject``, ``uninject``, "
"``expose``, ``unexpose``, ``pin``, ``unpin``, ``upgrade``, ``upgrade-all``, "
"``upgrade-shared``, ``uninstall``, ``uninstall-all``, ``reinstall``, "
"``reinstall-all``, ``reset``, ``health``, ``repair``, ``manifest lock``, "
"``manifest sync``, ``interpreter list``, ``interpreter prune``, "
"``interpreter upgrade``, ``cache dir``, and ``cache purge``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:59
msgid ""
"It is not available on ``install-all``, ``run``, ``exec``, ``runpip``, "
"``ensurepath``, ``environment``, ``completions``, or ``help``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:64
msgid "``list`` is different"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:66
msgid ""
"``pipx list --output json`` does not emit the result envelope. It prints the "
"installed-package snapshot that ``install-all`` reads back: an object with "
"``pipx_spec_version`` and a ``venvs`` map of environment name to its "
"metadata (see :doc:`metadata`). ``pipx list --json`` is a legacy alias for "
"the same snapshot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:70
msgid ""
"$ pipx list --output json > pipx.json\n"
"$ pipx install-all pipx.json"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:75
msgid ""
"``--json`` is a legacy alias only on ``list``; every other command uses ``--"
"output json``."
msgstr ""
